  "findings": [
    "Exact CPU table: 06_97 stepping 0,1,2,4,5; 06_9A stepping 1,2,3,4. 11-bit IccMax and Alder Lake VR descriptor. hasUnlimitedIccMaxFlag is 0.",
    "IA PCORE/RING/ECORE share bits 11:8 address and bit 12 SVID descriptor. Platform.c interprets a clear flag as SVID.",
    "GT descriptors have inconsistent mask/shift comments. GT and SA are excluded, not inferred from adjacent entries.",
    "VFTuning.c commands 16/17 use the VR address, quarter-amp raw values, and separate unlimited bit31.",
    "Intel Alder Lake FSP documents IA 1/4 A increments. Config structure offsets are not hardware addresses.",
    "No B7 profile inferred from Alder Lake sources. No unlimited-mode setter, zero/default setting, MSR601 write, hardware execution or claims of physical validation.",
    "VFTuning ADL bit31 comment conflicts with CPU table hasUnlimitedIccMaxFlag=0. No verified unlimited-mode semantics published: expose bit31, block editing when set, preserve it unchanged."
  ]
